### RPC handlers that can trigger outbound HTTP to user-configured webhook URLs

These are implemented on `APIV1Service` and exposed via `ConnectServiceHandler` with the same method names (`server/router/api/v1/connect_handler.go`, `connect_services.go`).

| Handler | File | Trigger chain |
|---------|------|---------------|
| **`CreateMemo`** | `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:157` | `DispatchMemoCreatedWebhook` → `dispatchMemoRelatedWebhook` → `webhook.PostAsync` → `Post` |
| **`UpdateMemo`** | `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:513` | `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects` → `DispatchMemoUpdatedWebhook` → `dispatchMemoRelatedWebhook` → `webhook.PostAsync` → `Post` |
| **`DeleteMemo`** | `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:562` | `DispatchMemoDeletedWebhook` → `dispatchMemoRelatedWebhook` → `webhook.PostAsync` → `Post` |
| **`CreateMemoComment`** | `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go:119` | `DispatchMemoCommentCreatedWebhook` → `webhook.PostAsync` → `Post` (also calls `CreateMemo` internally, which can fire a created webhook for the comment author) |
| **`SetMemoAttachments`** | `server/router/api/v1/memo_attachment_service.go:48` | `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects` → updated webhook path above |
| **`SetMemoRelations`** | `server/router/api/v1/memo_relation_service.go:48` | same updated webhook path |

Webhook dispatch helpers in `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_webhooks.go`:

